#X text 215 83 Duffing Attractor;
#X text 215 108 Written by Paul Bourke;
#X text 215 133 ---;
#X text 215 158 The solution to the Duffing equations is often used
as an example of a classic chaotic system.;
#X text 215 198 The Duffing system of differential equations is:;
#X text 215 223 ===========;
#X text 215 248 dx / dt = y;
#X text 215 273 dy / dt = x - x3 - a y + b cos(w t);
#X text 215 298 ===================================;
#X text 215 323 where typically \, a = 0.25 \, b = 0.3 \, w = 1;
#X text 215 348 The following shows a "typical" segment of (x \, y)
values.;
